1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,540
Robots learn to grasp
from human demonstrations.

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:07,340
But through a teleoperation
glove, you feel nothing.

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:12,270
So many demos end as drops and crushes,
and someone sorts them by hand.

4
00:00:12,487 --> 00:00:15,687
Egg Shell: a Rokoko glove
stream drives a Shadow

5
00:00:15,687 --> 00:00:20,387
robot hand in MuJoCo,
with an egg that can crack.

6
00:00:20,387 --> 00:00:23,967
The glove input here is
simulated: a scripted operator,

7
00:00:23,967 --> 00:00:27,517
through the same pipeline
as real glove data.

8
00:00:27,753 --> 00:00:29,853
Here is the wire path.

9
00:00:29,853 --> 00:00:32,913
Rokoko's hand solver serves RGMP version

10
00:00:32,913 --> 00:00:36,913
two on TCP port twelve two seven seven.

11
00:00:36,913 --> 00:00:39,713
Type one messages define the stream.

12
00:00:39,713 --> 00:00:45,813
Type two carry twenty-six OpenXR joints,
each a position and a rotation.

13
00:00:45,813 --> 00:00:49,363
Our client reads them directly,
with no ROS install.

14
00:00:49,653 --> 00:00:51,133
Then retargeting.

15
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:55,513
Frames turn Z-up, and a yaw
calibration points the fingers forward.

16
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:58,473
Each angle comes from a
bone relative to its parent,

17
00:00:58,473 --> 00:01:01,113
so hand position does not change it.

18
00:01:01,113 --> 00:01:03,733
A flat hand, held for five seconds,

19
00:01:03,733 --> 00:01:08,073
sets each person's zero, and
a filter smooths the noise.

20
00:01:08,093 --> 00:01:11,653
Twenty-one human angles become
twenty Shadow actuators,

21
00:01:11,653 --> 00:01:14,403
six Inspire values and a wrist target.

22
00:01:14,653 --> 00:01:16,253
A careful try.

23
00:01:16,253 --> 00:01:18,373
The hand lifts the egg eleven centimetres,

24
00:01:18,373 --> 00:01:22,523
at a peak grip force of three
point seven six newtons.

25
00:01:22,787 --> 00:01:24,647
Now a squeeze.

26
00:01:24,707 --> 00:01:27,287
Force reaches nineteen point six newtons,

27
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:31,107
past the crack threshold of
eight, and the egg turns red.

28
00:01:31,107 --> 00:01:34,917
That threshold is a simulation
proxy, not a measured egg.

29
00:01:35,087 --> 00:01:37,467
Every try is saved as a training episode,

30
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:41,227
with grip force per frame
and a simulator label.

31
00:01:41,227 --> 00:01:42,007
Lifted.

32
00:01:42,007 --> 00:01:42,727
Crushed.

33
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:43,567
Lifted.

34
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:44,617
Not lifted.

35
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:49,160
Each episode file holds ten
arrays, one row per step:

36
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,960
time, raw glove frames, human angles,

37
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:55,200
actions, wrist target, Inspire commands,

38
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:59,080
joint positions, hand pose,
egg pose and egg force.

39
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,250
The actions and the wrist
target are enough to replay it.

40
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,200
But thresholds miss things.

41
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:08,900
The third egg rose ten point nine
centimetres, so the simulator says lifted.

42
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,120
Then the hand opened in the air.

43
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:15,600
NVIDIA Nemotron reviews each episode
from keyframes and the force log.

44
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:19,580
Verdict: dropped, confidence
zero point nine eight.

45
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:23,780
Grip force hit zero with the egg
three point four centimetres up.

46
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:26,120
The episode is flagged for a human.

47
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,010
The simulator label stays.

48
00:02:28,287 --> 00:02:30,387
The review step by step.

49
00:02:30,387 --> 00:02:33,967
Nemotron gets four keyframes,
from first contact to the end,

50
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:37,687
and a twenty-four row
force and lift timeline.

51
00:02:37,687 --> 00:02:43,467
It must answer in strict JSON, citing
a frame or the log for each claim.

52
00:02:43,467 --> 00:02:46,327
A bad schema gets one repair request.

53
00:02:46,327 --> 00:02:49,647
A grounding check compares
its numbers with the log.

54
00:02:49,647 --> 00:02:52,127
Then the cross-check with the simulator.

55
00:02:52,127 --> 00:02:55,687
One bug we hit: with a
twelve-hundred-token budget,

56
00:02:55,687 --> 00:02:59,667
the model spent it all
reasoning and replied empty.

57
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:04,457
Now it gets four thousand ninety-six,
and empty replies are never cached.

58
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:07,180
Nemotron agrees on three of four,

59
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:11,620
and four episodes is a smoke
test, not an accuracy figure.

60
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,440
Fifty-two tests pass.

61
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:19,700
Our client speaks Rokoko's RGMP wire
format, and round-trips joint angles.

62
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,390
Replay gives the same label, four of four.

63
00:03:22,587 --> 00:03:25,287
What is verified, and what is not.

64
00:03:25,287 --> 00:03:29,747
Verified with no gloves: the wire
format against Rokoko's bridge code,

65
00:03:29,747 --> 00:03:34,167
the angle maths, the MuJoCo
hand, labels and replay.

66
00:03:34,167 --> 00:03:37,227
Still needs hardware: real Smartglove data,

67
00:03:37,227 --> 00:03:41,467
the ROS 2 path, the live viewer,
and a real Inspire hand.

68
00:03:41,467 --> 00:03:43,737
And the crack threshold stays a proxy.

69
00:03:44,087 --> 00:03:46,567
The labels make the data trainable.

70
00:03:46,567 --> 00:03:51,127
We trained a small policy on four
hundred eighty scripted demonstrations,

71
00:03:51,127 --> 00:03:56,587
then fine-tuned one copy on the lifted
ones and one on the crushed ones.

72
00:03:56,587 --> 00:03:59,327
The difference in weights is a task vector.

73
00:03:59,327 --> 00:04:01,427
Add the lifted vector, with no new training,

74
00:04:01,427 --> 00:04:04,007
and success on unseen eggs goes from

75
00:04:04,007 --> 00:04:06,027
twenty-seven to sixty-seven percent,

76
00:04:06,027 --> 00:04:09,547
while crushes fall from
sixty-two to twenty-eight.

77
00:04:09,547 --> 00:04:12,467
Add the crushed vector, and
crushes rise to eighty-three.

78
00:04:12,467 --> 00:04:18,267
Not everything works: subtracting
the crushed vector breaks the reach.

79
00:04:18,287 --> 00:04:21,337
Scripted demonstrations, simulated egg.

80
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:25,293
Next: real Rokoko gloves at the venue,

81
00:04:25,293 --> 00:04:28,213
Inspire hand commands sent to a real hand,

82
00:04:28,213 --> 00:04:32,483
and a behaviour-cloning policy
trained on clean episodes only.

83
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,560
Egg Shell.

84
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:35,590
The robot feels what you can't.

